# Buddy auth and secrets

Human guide: `docs/auth.md`. Session pick is `ResolveSession` in `internal/buddy/session.go`.

- Config is `tenant:` (`default`) + `tenants:` + `auths:` + optional `channels:` policies (legacy string tenant/defaults/allow_auths/credentials migrate on load). Selection: `--tenant` (auto-pick) or `--user`/`--auth` (pin). Auth `channels:` limits buddy clients `cli|mcp|ide` (omit = all). Top-level `channels.<client>` sets `access` / `tenant` / `tenants` allowlist, optional `deny_builtins`, and optional `allow_builtins` (allow follows deny). The same deny/allow lists are valid on `tenants.` and `auths.`; layers are independent (channel allow cannot unblock a tenant deny). MCP always denies `jamf_*` on the channel layer unless `allow_builtins` unblocks it. `deny_builtins: ["*"]` is an allowlist at that layer. Cowboy channel override: `allow_builtins: ["*"]`.
- macOS org defaults: Jamf ACS/MCX preference domain `virtualpete.buddy.cli` (or `BUDDY_MANAGED_PLIST`) overlays onto user `config.yaml` (user wins per name). Auths in the plist are accepted if present; `buddy setup managed-plist` omits them. Prefer `buddy setup secrets` for the store. `SaveConfig` does not snapshot unmodified MDM keys.
- Token logic lives in `internal/buddy/tokenauth/`; process cache in `common.go` (`credAuthCache` keyed `auth@tenant`); disk cache in `~/.config/buddy/tokens/` (AES-GCM obfuscated with compiled key; skipped for command auth).
- Secrets: inline config wins, then `secrets.DefaultStore()` (Keychain macOS, file Linux, or `BUDDY_SECRET_STORE`), keyed by **auth name**.
- Resolve via `CredentialConfig.ResolveAuthWithSecrets` (composed tenant+auth view) before building an `Authenticator`.
- CLI: `buddy auth token|refresh|test|caps`, `buddy cred status|add`, `buddy cred set tenant|auth|channel|secret …` (`--channels=`), `buddy cred delete tenant|auth|secret …` (cascade + store secrets), `buddy cred clean secrets|tokens`, `buddy cred erase secrets`, `buddy cred backup|restore <file>`, `buddy cred use [--cli|--mcp|--ide]`, `buddy cred store`, `buddy cred migrate`.
- Token refresh: reuse until expiry (minus ~15s skew). Keep-alive is **basic auth only** on 401 / `buddy auth refresh`. OAuth re-auths via client credentials when expired or on 401. Authenticated HTTP retries once on 401 after refresh. Disk token files are purged when expired (`cred clean tokens` or on load miss).
- Live checks: `buddy auth test` always ForceRenews (instance and platform). Probe 403 after a minted token is `live=token-ok`, not a bad secret. Last results + instance privileges are cached under `~/.config/buddy/caps/` and used by session pick (fail open). `cred get secret` is presence only.
- buddyscript/MCP session kwargs are `tenant?` / `surface?` / `auth?` (`cred` removed). Soft-switch on auth pin alone is a fallback when the implicit tenant is not linked. A readonly pin falls back to a full-access auth on the same tenant for mutates; channel `access: readonly` does not. Classic follows a platform pin by default (`/api/proclassic/tenant/{id}/…` with `/JSSResource` stripped). Set `features.classic_instance_only: true` or `BUDDY_CLASSIC_INSTANCE_ONLY=true` to force Classic onto instance. That toggle is Classic `/JSSResource` only. ACS `/api/config-profiles/` and undocumented Pro `GET /api/v1/policies` are always instance (Jamf Pro UI / unpublished JSON; not on the gateway).
